CLOUDEAGLE DEVELOPER INTEGRATION STUDIO — MASTER BUILD PROMPT
ROLE AND NON-NEGOTIABLE OBJECTIVE
Act as a principal product designer, staff full-stack engineer, AI agent architect, enterprise security engineer, and senior QA automation engineer. Build a polished, actually interactive, developer-facing web application named CloudEagle Developer Integration Studio with the positioning “From API documentation to trustworthy integration code—with developers in control.”

This is for developers building integrations. Do not build a generic SaaS administrator dashboard, chatbot landing page, or static slideshow. The developer must be able to onboard, browse categorized integrations, create and own integrations through a conversational flow, validate API documentation, select a company-provided model, supervise a resumable multi-agent code-generation run, approve checkpoints, inspect/edit/save generated code, see success/failure results, and open full redacted traces for debugging.

Use the user's requirements as the canonical functional specification. Prioritize a complete, functioning Calendly demo plus rigorous negative/error scenarios over ornamental features. Do not falsely claim live functionality if it is a simulation.
TECHNOLOGY / RUNTIME
- Use Google AI Studio Build > Web app full-stack runtime: React + TypeScript frontend and Node.js TypeScript backend.
- Use Tailwind CSS and a high-quality accessible component set, Lucide-style icons, a code editor (Monaco if compatible; otherwise CodeMirror or a robust syntax-highlighted editor), clean charts only if necessary.
- Keep Gemini/provider calls, documentation URL fetching, and secrets on the server. Use the official Google Gen AI SDK (@google/genai) when Gemini is configured. Obtain the configured model ID dynamically from the server model registry; do not hardcode an unverified/current model name.
