- Use a persistent store for users, integrations, categories, integration files/versions, generation runs, checkpoints, approvals, and trace events. Prefer Firestore if available; for a local preview use a compact server persistence mechanism; localStorage/IndexedDB may back demo data only if server persistence isn't configured. All access-control checks must be enforced server-side in any connected/multiuser mode. No secrets in browser persistence.
- Produce the frontend, backend endpoints, fixture data, generated code ZIP export, README, and tests. Ensure the project compiles and every primary control works.
